Vendored: src/*.ts are the files of src/vdb/ (parseVdb and its helpers). src/nanovdb/ (P13-H4) holds the package's NanoVDB dense
builder, Fp8 quantizer and .nvdb writer (bytes, tree, stats, leaf-codec, serialize, quantize, write-nvdb: unchanged; index.ts trimmed to
those exports), used by exportFineNvdb in @clouds/runtime/import. buildFromVdb, transform and inspect are not vendored.

Changes from upstream (made for the Nubis cloud importer, P4-H):
- parse.ts: optional second argument `{ select }`. After a grid's metadata and transform are read, `select(descriptor)`
  decides whether to decode its tree; skipped grids are listed in `VdbFile.descriptors` without decoding (so a first
  pass can list names, classes, voxel sizes and bounds cheaply). Unsupported grids no longer abort the whole file when
  they are not selected. Each descriptor records compression flags (blosc/zip) and the grid class.
- tree.ts, grid.ts, types.ts: constant-value tiles at the lower (8^3) and upper (128^3) node level are kept
  (`VdbGrid.tiles`) instead of being dropped or rejected, so level sets with an inactive negative interior and fog
  volumes with active tiles read correctly. Active root-level tiles are still rejected.
- tree.ts: files older than 222 store a leaf's origin and buffer count after its value mask (OpenVDB LeafNode::readBuffers); upstream
  read them before it, which broke the 2013-era bunny_cloud.vdb (file version 220).
- compression.ts: inactive-value defaults follow OpenVDB (background / -background instead of 0), so level sets whose inactive interior
  is -background decode correctly; lz4 Blosc chunks are decoded through the new blosc.ts instead of raising an error.
- blosc.ts (new, not from upstream): Blosc 1.x chunk decoder, lz4 codec, with byte shuffle and split streams. Other codecs
  (blosclz, snappy, zlib, zstd) and bit shuffle raise VdbUnsupportedError naming the codec.
